cards.agent_description:
Onboard and configure a Loyalty Program Partner for a Salesforce Loyalty program — create the
LoyaltyProgramPartner, LoyaltyPgmPartnerCurrency, and LoyaltyPartnerProduct records through the
Headless 360 MCP (discover/describe/dispatch over the Salesforce REST Data API, never a local
command-line client). Use this for ANY loyalty partner setup, including these exact requests:
  • an accrual partner / a partner of only accrual / accrual-only partner;
  • a redemption partner / a partner of only redemption / redemption-only partner;
  • a partner that is both accrual and redemption (a "both" partner), or two partners — one accrual
    and one redemption, or two partners with both;
  • a prepaid partner and its prepaid points pack (LoyaltyPgmPtnrPrepaidPack), and postpaid partners;
  • a joint promotion co-funded by two or more partners, splitting contribution percentages
    (e.g. 20:80, 50:50) — the co-funding junction (LoyaltyPgmPartnerPromotion, ContributionPercentage)
    and its activate-at-100% gate;
  • partner currencies, partner products, and accrual/redemption conversion factors.
This is the "loyalty-program-partner-setup" B2B partner onboarding flow (partner accrual, partner
redemption, prepaid/postpaid billing, joint/co-funded promotions). Requires an existing LoyaltyProgram
(run loyalty-program-lifecycle-setup first) and Loyalty Partner Management enabled in the org.

query_params.q:
SELECT FIELDS(STANDARD), Account.Name, SalesChannel.SalesChannelName
FROM OrderSummary
WHERE OrderedDate >= {startDate}
  AND OrderedDate <= {endDate}
ORDER BY OrderedDate DESC, Id DESC
LIMIT 21

SELECT FIELDS(STANDARD), Account.Name, SalesChannel.SalesChannelName,
       {customFieldApiName}
FROM OrderSummary
WHERE {customFieldClause}
ORDER BY OrderedDate DESC, Id DESC
LIMIT 21

{priorQuery}
AND (OrderedDate < {cursorDate}
     OR (OrderedDate = {cursorDate} AND Id < '{cursorId}'))
ORDER BY OrderedDate DESC, Id DESC
LIMIT 21
